{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1729, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nThere are N black balls and M white balls.\r\nEach ball has a value. The value of the i-th black ball (1 \\le i \\le N) is B_i, and the value of the j-th white ball (1 \\le j \\le M) is W_j.\nChoose zero or more balls so that the number of black balls chosen is at least the number of white balls chosen. Among all such choices, find the maximum possible sum of the values of the chosen balls.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN M\r\nB_1 B_2 \\ldots B_N\r\nW_1 W_2 \\ldots W_M\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1 \\leq N,M \\leq 2\\times 10^5\n- -10^9 \\leq B_i, W_j \\leq 10^9\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n4 3\r\n8 5 -1 3\r\n3 -2 -4\n\nSample Output 1\n\n19\r\n\nIf you choose the 1st, 2nd, and 4th black balls, and the 1st white ball, the sum of their values is 8+5+3+3=19, which is the maximum.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n4 3\r\n5 -10 -2 -5\r\n8 1 4\n\nSample Output 2\n\n15\r\n\nIf you choose the 1st and 3rd black balls, and the 1st and 3rd white balls, the sum of their values is 5+(-2)+8+4=15, which is the maximum.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n3 5\r\n-36 -33 -31\r\n12 12 28 24 27\n\nSample Output 3\n\n0\r\n\nIt is possible to choose no balls.\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1779, "char_start": 1741, "quote": "Input:\n4 3\n8 5 -1 3\n3 -2 -4\nOutput:\n19", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1830, "char_start": 1791, "quote": "Input:\n4 3\n5 -10 -2 -5\n8 1 4\nOutput:\n15", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1889, "char_start": 1842, "quote": "Input:\n3 5\n-36 -33 -31\n12 12 28 24 27\nOutput:\n0", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "eac4ee5b9e042d965912b14e02441d6111a0e677508a22f7cd490b33d33c67d1", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "65d11f27675dd4714a3c473cda2a79c16e5d41f500610b4187e61c7cf149cb78", "seq": 2}
